 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "arr is a non-empty list of non-negative integers with at least one positive element. One operation lowers one element by 1. A target array is bitonic when it is zero outside one contiguous block and that block reads 1, 2, ..., k - 1, k, k - 1, ..., 2, 1 for some k >= 1 (adjacent block values differ by exactly 1). Return the minimum number of operations that turn arr into a bitonic array, which is sum(arr) minus the largest k * k over all blocks that fit under arr.",
